## 3. Inert backdrop rule (don't break drag-pan with bottom sheets)

The directions panel (`MapMarkerDirectionsPanel`) and POI sheet (`MapMarkerPoiSheet`) are bottom sheets that visually cover the lower portion of the bird-eye view. If their root (or a transparent backdrop element) had `pointer-events: auto`, the area between the top of the sheet and the top of the viewport would silently swallow touch / mouse drag events — the user could no longer drag-pan the map above the panel.

### Required pattern

- The panel's root wrapper has `pointer-events: none`
- Only the visible bottom sheet itself has `pointer-events: auto`
- **No tap-outside-to-close backdrop element.** Dismiss is via the visible X / back buttons inside the sheet header.

CSS:

```css
.map-marker-directions {
  position: fixed;
  inset: 0;
  pointer-events: none;          /* root: inert */
}
.map-marker-directions__sheet {
  /* ...positioning + visual styles... */
  pointer-events: auto;          /* only the sheet captures input */
}
```

`MapMarkerPoiSheet` follows the same contract but with one extra wrinkle: it reuses the `.cu-restroom-widget` class from `RestroomWidget.css`, which has `position: fixed; inset: 0;` (correct for the full-screen restroom panel — wrong for our bird-eye context). We can't change that shared class without breaking the restroom widget, so the POI sheet overrides at the inline-style level:

```tsx
<div className="cu-restroom-widget cu-restroom-widget--sheet-open"
     style={{ background: 'transparent', zIndex: 1200, pointerEvents: 'none' }}>
  <div className="cu-restroom-widget__sheet"
       style={{ pointerEvents: 'auto' }}>
    {/* ...sheet content... */}
  </div>
</div>
```

There is also no backdrop button. (`RestroomWidget` itself still uses an interactive backdrop because it appears in first-person view where there is no underlying drag-pan to preserve.)

> Anti-pattern: re-introducing a tap-outside-to-close `<button class="*-backdrop">` over the bird-eye stream silently breaks drag-pan above the sheet.
>
> Anti-pattern: forgetting the inline `pointerEvents` override on `MapMarkerPoiSheet` — the shared `.cu-restroom-widget` rule will silently capture the whole viewport even though the sheet looks fine, and the symptom is "tilt animates correctly but the map won't drag".

