## 4. Map-marker icon swap mirror

The directions panel has a swap button that flips the start / end inputs. The two endpoint markers on the bird-eye route overlay (start = white circle with dark-purple `MapPinSimpleArea.svg`; destination = lemon circle with dark-purple `flag-pennant.svg`) must follow that swap so the user sees a consistent "which end is the destination" indicator on the map.

### State lift

The `swapped` flag was lifted from a panel-local `useState` into the navigation hook so the overlay can read it:

| Field | Where | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `mapMarkerDirectionsSwapped` (state) | `usePoiNavigation.ts` | Default `false`. Reset to `false` inside `clearMapMarkerDirectionsPreview` and via a panel-side `useEffect` keyed on `previewRouteKey` so a previously swapped POI session does not carry into the next destination. |
| `setMapMarkerDirectionsSwapped` | exposed on the navigation context | Used by the panel's swap button toggle. |

### Overlay consumption

`BirdEyeRouteOverlay.tsx`:

```tsx
const swapped = nav.mapMarkerDirectionsSwapped;
// start bubble (geometric first point)
<img src={swapped ? flagPennantUrl : mapPinUrl} ... />
// destination bubble (geometric last point)
<img src={swapped ? mapPinUrl : flagPennantUrl} ... />
```

The route polyline geometry is always Kit's `first → last` path; only the icons swap. Bubble background colours stay tied to the geometric position (white start ring, lemon destination ring) — they don't follow the swap, so a swapped destination is "lemon ring with map pin" and a swapped start is "white ring with flag". This matches the panel's tab styling where the icons swap but the field colours don't.

