## 5. Pan to center a world target (no route, no camera rotation change)

**Kit:** `younite.usd_viewer_player_core_extension` — event **`birdEyePanFocusWorld`** with payload **`worldPos`**: `[x, y, z]` in scene units (same as other world-space messages). Handler `_bird_eye_pan_focus_world` runs only when `viewType === birdEye`: intersects the active viewport camera’s **center ray** with the horizontal plane `y = worldPos[1]`, then adds the XZ delta to the **player prim’s translate op** (same mechanism as drag-pan in `BirdEyeUsdTranslateMover`). Camera **RotateXYZ** is not modified.

**Web (dev IoT menu):** `TransitLiveDevSection.tsx` — live transit rows (bird-eye only) send **`birdEyeRouteClear`** then **`birdEyePanFocusWorld`** so a prior `birdEyeRouteRequest` preview line does not linger. See `transit-live-overlay.mdc`.

**Kit (IoT station list):** `younite.open_data_live_extension` — on **`iotAirQualityFocusStation`** in bird-eye, dispatches the same two events (after lat/lon → scene XYZ) so air-quality “focus” uses **player_core** `_bird_eye_pan_focus_world` — no second pan implementation.

