## Events summary

| Event | Direction | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `birdEyeFrameTarget` | Web → Kit | Begin cinematic tilt-down animation |
| `birdEyeFrameRestore` | Web → Kit | Animate back to the spawn pitch |
| `touchLookDelta` | Web → Kit | Pointer drag — FP look (`tick`) or bird-eye pan (`tick_bird_eye_pan`) |
| `touchLookEnd` | Web → Kit | Pointer-up after pan/look drag — arms FP look coast + bird-eye pan coast (`touch-look.mdc`) |
| `birdEyeYawDelta` | Web → Kit | `{ deltaDeg }` — incremental map rotation while twisting / rotate-dragging |
| `birdEyeYawEnd` | Web → Kit | Pointer-up after twist or rotate-drag — arms map rotation release coast |
| `birdEyeZoomLevel` | Web → Kit | `{ level }` — pinch / wheel zoom (focalLength) |
| `birdEyePanFocusWorld` | Web → Kit | `{ worldPos: [x,y,z] }` — pan rig so target lies on view-center ray (bird-eye only; see §5) |

No outbound events from the framer — the tilt is fire-and-forget from the panel's `useEffect`.

